Z||000019||Sleeper||01-16-2001||08:58 PM||||nope, i got mine in a little rim shop in L.A., if you go to your nearest discount/americas tire center they can order them for you plus shipping. my c5's cost me about $1400 rims, tires and everything and I shopped around for a good 2 months looking for the best deals(c5's weren't the only rims i was looking at and after buying the rims I was sick of looking at rims all together). c5's usually cost about $1700 to $1800 depending on the size 17 or 18 you just have to take your time and shop around.<P>oh, my tires are Kumho Ecsta Supra 712, 215/40/17's in the front and 225/45/17's in the rear. dope little tires.<p>[This message has been edited by Sleeper (edited 01-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||G-Nasty||01-17-2001||11:08 PM||||I have the ultimate setup using bel-tec 2" drop spindles and lowered rear springs by suspension techniques(the jap car guys). The car has 16" O.Z. corsa in front w/ Yokamomma 215 45 17 and 17" corsa rims on rear. Yokahoma ZR 235 45 17!!! They no longer sell these forged 6 spoke rims which makes them super rare. CARPARTS.COM and J.C. whitney sells the spindles and springs. U- must lower the car otherwise it will look wrong. ||||reg||1
Z||000021||G-Nasty||01-17-2001||11:17 PM||||I have no clearance problems with the 235 45 17's in the rear and with the front 215 45 16's. I get a lot of complementz and I will post a pic soon or email me for the most radical Italian/Austrian forged rims made for these cars- ||||reg||1
