Z||000023||Slammed Fiero||01-25-2001||10:29 AM||||The little picture on my signature is craptacular , but it shows my TRmotorsports typhoons with 255/40/17's in the rear , and 225/45/17's front , Pirelli P zero C's Ti doesn't rub in the rear , I have coil overs though thus the strut collar has been ground down quite a bit. It's still close , but after a few track sessions there have been no problems with it rubbing<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||Slammed Fiero||01-25-2001||10:45 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/gtashow.JPG"> <P>here's a better pic<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000025||Wade87GT||01-25-2001||11:07 AM||||Hey Slammed,<P>What did you use to lower your front end and how does it ride? Details please?<P>Wade||||reg||5
Z||000026||Slammed Fiero||01-25-2001||12:34 PM||||The front end has Koni's on it and a set of Carrera springs , I had a set of fiero store lowering springs and eibachs up front. Neither were what I wanted so I just ordered a custom rate. The ride is harsh on streets , but on a track it does'n tact like a fiero ,no understeer , just throttle induced oversteer. No trailing throttle oversteer either , ie when you lift in a corner it doesn't come around.<P>As for how low it is ...A coke can will not fit under the side of the car standing up.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
